WEBVTT

00:00.520 --> 00:01.680
Matthew 3

00:01.680 --> 00:07.000
In those days John the Baptist came preaching in the wilderness of Judea.

00:08.400 --> 00:11.720
Repent, for the kingdom of heaven is at hand.

00:12.580 --> 00:16.380
For this is he who was spoken of by the prophet Isaiah when he said,

00:17.260 --> 00:19.260
The voice of one crying in the wilderness,

00:20.020 --> 00:23.460
Prepare the way of the Lord, make his path straight.

00:24.200 --> 00:26.420
Now John wore a garment of camel's hair,

00:26.420 --> 00:31.160
and a leather belt around his waist, and his food was locusts and wild honey.

00:32.260 --> 00:37.080
Then Jerusalem and all Judea and all the region about the Jordan were going out to him,

00:37.340 --> 00:41.140
and they were baptized by him in the river Jordan, confessing their sins.

00:41.600 --> 00:46.200
But when he saw many of the Pharisees and Sadducees coming to his baptism,

00:46.540 --> 00:47.600
he said to them,

00:48.100 --> 00:54.600
You, brood of vipers, who warned you to flee from the wrath to come?

00:55.120 --> 00:56.400
Bear fruit and give me a son.

00:56.540 --> 00:57.500
Keep him with repentance.

00:58.220 --> 01:00.520
And do not presume to say to yourselves,

01:01.000 --> 01:03.960
We have Abraham as our father.

01:04.580 --> 01:09.560
For I tell you, God is able from these stones to raise up children for Abraham.

01:10.320 --> 01:13.440
Even now the axe is laid to the root of the trees.

01:13.800 --> 01:20.400
Every tree, therefore, that does not bear good fruit is cut down and thrown into the fire.

01:21.260 --> 01:23.660
I baptize you with water for repentance.

01:24.280 --> 01:26.400
But he who is coming after me is my son,

01:26.420 --> 01:30.100
and he is steadier than I, whose sandals I am not worthy to carry.

01:30.760 --> 01:34.060
He will baptize you with the Holy Spirit and fire.

01:34.800 --> 01:36.940
His winnowing fork is in his hand,

01:37.140 --> 01:42.020
and he will clear his threshing floor and gather his weed into the barn.

01:42.840 --> 01:46.200
But the chaff he will burn with unquenchable fire.

01:47.160 --> 01:51.720
Then Jesus came from Galilee to the Jordan to John, to be baptized by him.

01:52.280 --> 01:54.140
John would have prevented him, saying,

01:54.140 --> 01:56.200
I need to be baptized.

01:56.420 --> 01:59.320
I was baptized by you, and do you come to me?

02:00.120 --> 02:01.660
But Jesus answered him,

02:02.320 --> 02:06.560
Let it be so now, for thus it is fitting for us to fulfill all righteousness.

02:07.580 --> 02:08.900
Then he consented.

02:09.480 --> 02:13.520
And when Jesus was baptized, immediately he went up from the water,

02:13.620 --> 02:15.960
and behold, the heavens were opened to him,

02:16.040 --> 02:20.920
and he saw the Spirit of God descending like a dove and coming to rest on him.

02:21.080 --> 02:24.360
And behold, a voice from heaven said,

02:25.060 --> 02:29.620
This is my beloved Son, with whom I am well pleased.

02:29.620 --> 02:33.240
The End

